# The CLI is executed directly via its `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang. A CRLF
# ending makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named "node\r",
# so `npx t-perm` fails on Linux and macOS. Force LF on the executable script.
#
# Git already auto-detects binary files (verified: hand_landmarker.task
# round-trips byte-identical with core.autocrlf=true), so no rules are needed
# for *.task or *.glb.
bin/*.js text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
